userContent.text:
Build an interactive figure using SVG.js.

CONCEPT: In any oblique triangle the altitude h dropped from vertex β to the base b is the bridge to right-triangle trigonometry — h = c·sin(α) when α is acute, and h = c·sin(α′) on the extended base when α is obtuse, so the same area formula holds in both cases.
KEY INSIGHT (what students should walk away understanding): The altitude construction never fails — when the angle at α turns obtuse the perpendicular simply lands on an extension of the base, and because sin α′ = sin(180° − α) = sin α, the height h = c·sin α (and hence Area = ½ b c sin α) is the same formula in both cases.
DEMO STEPS: 6 guided steps — implement the step player in #ui

